# gate/concept.sh subject roster. Three columns: name, materialize-arm shape,
# demanded verdict (refused or pass). The roll is read from gate/concept.sh's
# own arms; a row naming a shape this gate cannot materialize, or a shape arm
# no row names, fails the ratchet. Zero rows examined fails (GAP-201).

# The utility bucket: two relations, each applied by its own subject, and no
# subject driving both. The produced refusal must reach this gate. Demanding
# `refused` is the NEGATIVE direction — a producer that stops refusing is
# convicted.
bucket bucket refused

# The passing cohort: one subject drives both relations; no row may be
# produced. Demanding `pass` is the POSITIVE direction — a producer that
# refuses a lawful cohort is convicted.
cohort cohort pass

# An unwitnessed module: nothing applies its one relation. No row may be
# produced — the adjudicator refuses a cohort sharing no demand, and one
# applied relation is not a cohort. This row is what stops the gate from
# reading every non-bucket as a bucket.
unwitnessed unwitnessed pass
